  "routingPrinciples":[
    "First decide whether generative video is necessary at all; deterministic Remotion/Lottie remains the default for factual, typographic and brand-critical content.",
    "Prefer a provider that can accept an approved first frame when composition continuity is important.",
    "Prefer first-last-frame control when a transition must land on a deterministic composition.",
    "Prefer video-to-video only for licensed/owned input footage and never to falsify documentary evidence.",
    "Do not route to a provider marked adapter-candidate as though it were executable from this repository.",
    "Provider capabilities are time-sensitive. Revalidate official documentation before implementing or enabling any adapter.",
    "Costs and quotas are not hard-coded into creative routing unless explicitly refreshed for a production decision."
